":"flow","items":["Literature Review","Research Question","Methodology","Participant Selection","Interviews/Primary Sources","Coding","Analysis","Interpretation","Conclusion"]},{"type":"p","text":"The researcher should distinguish between describing a religious tradition, interpreting it academically and making personal theological claims."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"This field requires particular care with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Respect for participants"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Representation of minority communities"},{"text":"Accurate quotation"},{"text":"Avoiding stereotyping"},{"text":"Distinguishing scholarship from advocacy"},{"text":"Proper handling of sacred or restricted materials"},{"text":"Transparent methodology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong researcher should approach religious traditions with academic neutrality and methodological discipline, regardless of personal beliefs."},{"type":"h","text":"Government / Public-Sector Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research-related opportunities can exist in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Archives"},{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Libraries"},{"text":"Cultural institutions"},{"text":"Heritage organisations"},{"text":"Research councils"},{"text":"Government cultural bodies"},{"text":"Educational institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact eligibility varies by post. Specialist academic and research positions commonly require postgraduate qualifications and research experience."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a serious research career, postgraduate study is strongly recommended."},{"type":"table","header":["PG","Best For"],"rows":[[{"text":"MA Theology"},{"text":"Theological research"}],[{"text":"MA Religious Studies"},{"text":"Comparative religion"}],[{"text":"MA Philosophy"},{"text":"Philosophy of religion"}],[{"text":"MA History"},{"